{
  "id": "ss.char.egg",
  "name": "Egg",
  "description": "The unhatched: the youngest of the brood and the one the fiction is least kind to, because its feelers were never given a signal to lose. Half the shell is still on its head, worn as a helm — off-white, the crack it came out through running down it, the broken edge zigzagging over the brow — with blond hair showing under it at the back. A padded gambeson of quilted bone-cloth, and over it a wrap of cocoon silk still wound across the chest; a short pale cloak. The feelers are stubs. Its weapon is what a squire carries: a pair of Soldier mandibles bound at the elbow, slung on the back with the jaws rising over the far shoulder, thrown so they come back. Same dead organ as the rest, set in the wrap. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
